{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as the complete ordinary evidence-only R1 revision6 design review at exact 667c3318d823e312c60e22bcfa059bbcfb16de9f, under invitation ceeaf521 and my promise061764af, preserving original requestc69b573d/promise8d614272 and Hugh's d4e07064 full demo/composable/all-component-retarget direction. This is design evidence only: no merge eligibility, implementation closure, sibling adoption or runtime proof.\n\nCoverage and identities: primary notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md artifactbddaa6bf,132192bytes2084lines,SHA256eb52db6a79b7b36a3600438ba45ea817538a3168c71bffde48b582e829077c52; corrections artifact353af040,22464bytes110lines,SHA256050ec30488731600714cbcf8d338ccb19c44f09c85f06a54e91b089038b3b05a; admission-read inventory artifact10a50aca,88015bytes420lines,SHA256a2b8f683ff81d48d3136d8a484da1dacc26f858709223c5b2bf6d75a5da7e26f. Verified all raw artifact records, exact head/path and sole builder-promise bases. Fresh registered detached checkout is clean at that head. The root transferred the previous complete revision5 main/correction reading only through a fully read 47309-byte575-line unified diff covering both changed files. The entire inventory is directly byte-equal to fully read revision5. No summary-only substitution. A parallel static reader independently checked all changed main/correction bytes and the central repairs. No tests/builds/installations/provider probes/private diagnostic or source implementation was performed.\n\nThe two P2 findings in e27f9b04 are closed in actual bytes. First, sections5.2/7.5 charge every timed selection immediately to one per-turn attempts budget, including head-stopped commits, dropped selections and alarm-only turns. A spent budget retains prior committed timed entries and all due work, writes no new outcome entry, answers a waiting act busy without consuming its key, retries a delivery with its duty retained, and reschedules an alarm. The repeated selection-clock5/commit-clock4/previous-time3 witness now terminates; the seventy-due-holds witness retains the first64 and drains the remaining6 next turn. The value64 and alarm retry delay remain proposals owed to R4, not measured results.\n\nSecond, section6.4 explicitly rejects genesis-timed at definition validation whenever the genesis opens a timed item type or has a hold effect; replay applies the same rule. Timed type includes any type with a timed rule even if opening sets no deadline. This removes the provisional-child deadline/confirmation conflict. Ordinary genesis time values remain legal when no timed rule reads them, and held duties remain held until activation. The R2 revision6 file/open genesis witnesses need no timed genesis, without adopting R2 or R3.\n\nThe range-guard clarification is also closed: section6.5 defines a completed Boolean evaluation by sufficient witnesses, with an exact table. Existential truth, absence failure, satisfied lower bound and exceeded upper bound can be witnessed. Successful absence, successful upper bound, and exact counts require complete evidence. A count with both bounds cannot pass without complete evidence. Unfinished inconclusive evaluation remains guard-incomplete/retry, and replay derives the same Boolean from all folded items.\n\nNonblocking editorial clarifications:1728–1730 says a turn ending busy wrote no entry, whereas513–515 correctly keep timed entries already committed in that turn. Say that no entry records the busy outcome or dropped selection. Also make the exact-budget boundary explicit:415–423 allows an ordinary input when no due item remains, while463 says a spent count ends the turn. State whether consuming the final allowed timed attempt ends immediately or permits the waiting input once the drain is empty. Either choice preserves the finite-turn and expiry-order invariants; align the prose and a boundary witness.\n\nArchitecture: The full contract remains coherent as a proposed local fold and replay design. It preserves fixed first-version placement, scope/incarnation/four reference classes, exact historical fact versus current grant versus operation identity, immutable selected contribution provenance, source-owned relationships, causal parent/child verification, missing/unsupported outcomes, bounded range/time dependencies, and explicit rewrite/deletion ownership. No new architectural blocker was found in this revision. Five sibling requests are now precisely listed with sources and remain unresolved, including send counts, settlement terminality, pin addressing, preparation-side staging and the register's directory confirmation. Design approval does not silently answer them.\n\nSecurity: The repaired drain cannot admit an ordinary entry ahead of a due expiry; validation and replay prevent a deadline in a provisional genesis; range guards never establish an overturnable result from partial evidence. Authenticated remote outcomes remain separate from transport replies and trusted attempt logs. Historical provenance remains separate from continuing authority. Unknown external effects and real credential/operation duties still require reconciliation and cannot disappear by reset. No new security blocker found in reviewed bytes.\n\nSimplification: A single timed-attempt budget, one shared validation/replay genesis exclusion, and a small Boolean-witness table resolve the defects without another timer queue, compatibility path or identity map. Keep those rules in the public model. The actual contract/policy/log/verifier/Room/client source successors and deletions remain assigned acceptance work, not delivered implementation.\n\nScope/dependencies retained: All original R1 duties remain, including complete local guard audit and reusable public-primitives demonstrations, the 10x test-economy direction, every affected export/storage/config/test owner, and proper personal reconciliation of the prior S1 commitment rather than inference from planner cancellation. R0's complete demo and R2/R3/R4 remain separately reviewed/adopted work. Current R2 preliminary findings c18a0413 and newly announced R2rev7/R3rev5 are not closed or adopted here. Numerical guard/retention/entry/reserve/send budgets and measured costs are still owed to R4. No legacy Artroom format/API/schema/client, old engine, adapter, dual architecture, identity mapping or pre-change replay preservation is required. New-model replay, exact provenance and real unresolved duties remain required. Schedule estimates do not reduce functional scope.\n\nAcknowledged current head news: builder67f495a9 announces R1rev6 filed while R2rev7/R3rev5 remain unfiled and R4rev4 partial. This approval rests on the exact three R1 artifacts and the accepted ordinary review route only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bddaa6bfd72016543d61e0be24e2344ef0728228","binding":"evidence-only","head":"667c3318d823e312c60e22bcfa059bbcfb16de9f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:061764af7181866ae3277286d35ae985eefc13a4\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4c9045171ad6ae81aa489585df3b0d361e40a9cf","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}